# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The catch-all must come LAST and must not shadow the prerendered files. Every
# route in the sitemap is written to disk as real HTML by scripts/prerender.mjs,
# and a rewrite placed above them serves the home page for all 53 — which looks
# fine locally and is invisible until somebody checks what Google indexed.
#
# `200!` would force the rewrite even when a file exists. That is exactly what
# must not happen here, so it is a plain 200: the file wins, and this only
# catches the client-side routes that have no file — cart, checkout, account,
# search, admin.
/*    /index.html   200
